The statement of Erdős Problem 612 in ErdosLean/Erdos612/Statement.lean was written
independently for this project. It follows the graphs-on-Fin-n convention of Formal Conjectures
(https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures) and is similar in shape to the draft by
Kenta Kitamura in formal-conjectures issue #828; no code or data from either source, or from
KitaKen1/erdos-612-lean, is included.

ErdosLean/Erdos514/* contains no third-party material: the statement was written from the problem
text on erdosproblems.com (google-deepmind/formal-conjectures has no file for Problem 514), and the
proof uses only Mathlib. ErdosLean/Erdos514/Statement.lean is original to this project and is not
derived from Formal Conjectures.

The Erdős Problem 956 files (ErdosLean/Erdos956/) do not include material from third-party code.
The statement was written from scratch from the problem text on erdosproblems.com. The
construction follows the mathematical note "Unit distances between disjoint convex translates"
(https://www.ulam.ai/research/erdos956.pdf, 27 April 2026). The note's mathematics is based on
the work of P. Valtr (Oberwolfach Reports 2 (2005), Report 17/2005;
https://kam.mff.cuni.cz/~valtr/n.pdf). No code from the note's accompanying Lean file was used.

